awalanche/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rawalanche/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T15:50:21Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T15:54:12Z","body":"> * This behavior is intentional, related [Hide the bottom panel when using distraction-free mode in the script editor godot-proposals#9141](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9141)\n\nIt does not matter whether it's intentional or not. It's simply bad. The mode does not do what it says it does, and the mode does not do what equivalent modes do in any other common sense software. There's simply no justification for this behavior other than irritating the user on purpose.\n\nThe link to the issue you sent rabbitholes all the way down to this request from 2020 https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/951 which was just one random opinionated suggestion from one random person, and it set of a cascade of bad decisions. What's concerning that such obviously bad UX regression made it through the code review and all the way into a final production release.\n\nThere is absolutely nothing preventing that one opinionated person who doesn't want the Distraction Free mode do what the label says to simply click the debug panel at the bottom to open it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4245282509/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eye